capability round/fraction  the part of a float after its point
  heroes  math.fraction
  go      Modf
  rust    f64::fract
  python  modf
  note    the whole part is `math.trunc`; an infinity's fraction is a zero, as C, Go and Python answer, where Rust's `fract` answers nan

capability round/to-integer  a float as an integer, or the failure that it does not fit
  heroes  built-in to_i64
  go      -
  rust    f64::to_int_checked, to_int_strict, to_int_saturating
  python  -
  note    `to_i64` truncates toward zero and fails `does_not_fit` for a nan, an infinity and a value outside i64; round first with `math.floor`, `math.ceil` or `math.round` for the other directions

capability round/decimal-digits  a float rounded to a count of decimal digits
  heroes  refused: the nearest float to a decimal rounding is found only by the conversion that writes the number as text, which is the package `numbers`'; `math` stands below it
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  round (with ndigits)

capability power/sqrt  the square root
  heroes  math.sqrt
  go      Sqrt
  rust    f64::sqrt
  python  sqrt
  note    a negative number answers nan, as C, Go and Rust; Python raises, and every function of this package answers IEEE's nan or infinity where Python raises a domain or a range error, since a `T?` on each call would make arithmetic unwritable and `math.is_nan` asks afterwards

capability power/cbrt  the cube root
  heroes  math.cbrt
  go      Cbrt
  rust    f64::cbrt
  python  cbrt
  note    the C library's root corrected by one Newton step whose residual is taken exactly by `fma`, so the answer is within a hair over half a unit of the true root on every platform (repaired 2026-11-18): glibc 2.41's `cbrt` answered -3.0000000000000004 for -27 in the Linux arm64 container, missed 2,264 of the 6,000 perfect cubes to 3000 cubed and the nearest float on 19,929 of 40,000 random inputs; Apple's missed no cube and 3,054 of the same inputs; the corrected root missed none on either, mpmath at 300 bits the oracle. C11 leaves the accuracy of `cbrt` to the implementation (5.2.4.2.2), so both libraries conform; the true root rounded once is the answer taken

capability power/hypot  the length of the longest side of a right triangle, with no overflow on the way
  heroes  math.hypot
  go      Hypot
  rust    f64::hypot
  python  hypot (two arguments)

